# === INFINI: user-uploaded media stays OUT of git ===
# All images/videos users upload while using the app are backed up to
# Cloudinary automatically by backup_sync.py (see storage.py / start.py),
# and restored from there on every deploy. Committing them to git as well
# caused GitHub's free Git LFS storage/bandwidth budget to be exceeded,
# which broke every deploy ("This repository exceeded its LFS budget").
# Only code needs to be in git — media does not.

# Generic: any folder literally named "uploads" anywhere in the tree
**/uploads/
**/uploads/**

# Known specific upload folders in this project (kept explicit too, in
# case a future refactor renames the generic "uploads" pattern above)
7000/ai_shop_uploads/
7000/id_entry_7000_uploads/
7000/id_home_uploads/
8046/ad_market_uploads/
8046/home_uploads/
8046/dashboard_uploads/

# NOTE: small auto-generated media under data/ folders (zone headers,
# scene images, a couple of story videos — ~1.5MB total) is deliberately
# KEPT in git, not excluded. backup_sync.py also backs these up to
# Cloudinary, but since deploys have failed repeatedly in the past it's
# not certain that backup ever ran successfully — excluding them here
# without a confirmed Cloudinary copy would risk losing them for good.
# They're tiny and no longer use Git LFS, so there's no cost to keeping
# them in git as a guaranteed copy.

# Local/dev artifacts that should never be committed
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
*.tmp

# Local test/session state (regenerated automatically at runtime)
8032/data/users.json
8032/data/infini_session_secret.txt
7000/id_entry_7000_state.json
star_trand_service/data/config.json
star_trand_service/data/memory.json

# Exception: 8046/uploads/normal_ad_media and normal_reward_media are NOT
# per-user ephemeral uploads — they're fixed-filename base/default media
# referenced directly by code (normal_ad_images.py / normal_reward_images.py)
# for the built-in ad/reward templates. Recovered real files, kept in git
# so the app has default images out of the box instead of empty templates.
!8046/uploads/
!8046/uploads/normal_ad_media/
!8046/uploads/normal_ad_media/**
!8046/uploads/normal_reward_media/
!8046/uploads/normal_reward_media/**

# Exception: recovered real uploads for user_bb290f5bb6f4, confirmed by
# cross-referencing 7000/data/user_spaces/user_bb290f5bb6f4/*.json — these
# filenames are actually referenced by that user's saved state (detail
# swipe cards, remote show, etc.), so without them those features show
# broken media. Kept in git as a guaranteed copy for the same reason as
# the small data/ media above (past deploys failed before Cloudinary
# backup could run, so there's no confirmed backup to restore from).
!7000/uploads/
!7000/uploads/user_bb290f5bb6f4/
!7000/uploads/user_bb290f5bb6f4/**
